# Fictional EP Tracklist

## Track 1: Revision Grid B-17

**Story & Context:** The debut track begins at 170 BPM with an almost untouched live drum break: kick, shallow snare, closed hat, one ride-bell accent, and two ghost notes before beat four. Maren, Elias, and Tomás enter with a four-voice Dorian block built from only five pitches. The crumhorns sustain mostly half- and quarter-note values, refusing to mirror the fast drum subdivisions.

After eight bars, Idris begins revising the break. The snare ghost before beat four is moved forward by a sixteenth, the second kick is replaced by a roomier alternate take, and a tom stroke is inserted where the listener previously heard silence. The reed voicing does not change. The effect is that the same chord suddenly appears to lean in a different direction even though no pitch or tempo has moved.

Saskia enters with a long violone fifth spanning sixteen bars. Pavel adds only three dulcimer events in the first minute: two damped clicks and one bright open course. At the midpoint, the crumhorn section begins substituting one note per cycle. The original chord slowly transforms into a suspended minor harmony without a single obvious change point.

The final passage reaches maximum drum complexity while the reeds simplify to one alto and one bass note. Idris assembles a dense but coherent break from dozens of slices taken from the same performance. The track ends when all edited percussion drops out and the listener hears the original uncut two-bar drum phrase once more under the final crumhorn dyad.

